\strong{Columns} (design 5.2), in the API's order: the fixed columns
(\code{dataset}, \code{provider_code}, \code{feature_id}, \code{profile_id}, \code{component_id},
\code{component_rank} integer, \code{horizon_id}, \code{horizon_name}, \code{upper_depth_cm},
\code{lower_depth_cm} double, \code{source_support}, \code{release_code}); with
\code{layer = "first"} \code{first_layer_status} and \code{profile_markings} (list of
character); the component columns when SOTWIS or SOTER polygons are
selected (\code{proportion_percent}, \code{cumulative_proportion_percent},
\code{terrain_proportion_percent} double, \code{is_representative},
\code{profile_inside_polygon} logical, \code{suid}, \code{tcid}, \code{scid} integer, the
others character); the source columns \code{source_profile_type} (SOTER:
\code{synthetic}, \code{virtual}), \code{source_record_note}, \verb{profile_attr_<key>} and
\verb{horizon_attr_<key>} (verbatim text: \code{horizon_attr_organic_surface} is
\code{"true"}/\code{"false"} as served); the raw markings (\code{texture_sum} double,
\code{consistency_flags} and \code{also_in_datasets} lists of character,
\code{possible_profile}, \code{superseded_by}, \code{cell_markings} a list of named
lists: variable column -> markings); \code{value_flags} (list of named lists:
variable column -> flags, \code{NULL} where none); \code{retired_in_release} (the
release in which the row's source left ISRIC, still served) and
\code{retired_cells} (named character: the cells retired while the row is
not); with \code{view = "revised"} \code{revised_markings} (named lists:
horizon markings, \code{hidden_values} a data frame \code{property_code}, \code{rule},
\code{source_value}, and \code{cells}); with \code{with_geometry = "text"}
\code{geometry_kind} and \code{geometry_text} (WKT, EPSG:4326, the geometry of the
row's feature); then, sorted by name, one group per variable: \verb{<key>}
(double when the column is numeric on every page, else the original text),
\verb{<key>_units}, \verb{<key>_method} (the laboratory method code of the value),
\verb{<key>_n} (integer: measurements collapsed into the cell, the first by
ingestion order is kept) and, for columns with multi-value cells,
\verb{<key>_values}. \verb{<key>} is the canonical property key (\code{organic_carbon});
source codes without a canonical mapping are \verb{src_<code>}. With
\code{with_geometry = "sf"} the result is an \code{sf} object whose \code{geometry}
column replaces \code{geometry_text}.

